# @@JSON GROUPING SUITE (2026-09-30)
#
# Grouping by a NESTED sub-column (a key inside an @@JSON cell, e.g. SUB_NAME)
# used to map each flat <tr> to its data by DOM POSITION (masterRowData[pos]).
# A flat sort moves the <tr>s in place, and an open journal note row pushes every
# row below it down one - so after either, rows landed in bands computed from
# OTHER rows' nested data, and "Sort groups by Summary" ranked bands on other
# rows' nested values. The fix resolves each row by its own '#' cell, like every
# other masterRowData reader.
#
# Each scenario boots the REAL main.js through the real run path (stubbed
# query.php) on a 240-row fixture, reorders the flat table the way a user does,
# groups through the REAL dialog, and checks every band against ground truth
# computed from the fixture alone (driver.js):
#   P-*  preconditions (the '#' premise, the sort/note row really happened, ...)
#   M-*  membership: a row sits only under names its own nested table holds
#   C-*  completeness: every eligible row under each of its names, exactly once
#   T-*  band totals ("of N") = whole-result counts
#   V-*  summary values; S-* band order under "Sort groups by Summary"
#
#   py -3 run.py                        candidate = live js\main.js
#   py -3 run.py --candidate F          any build (e.g. the stage copy before deploy)
#   py -3 run.py --control              candidate := the pre-fix baseline: EXACTLY the
#                                       CONTROL_RED asserts must fail, all others pass
#   py -3 run.py --mutant NAME          one fix site reverted in the candidate
#   py -3 run.py --mutants              every mutant, each against the asserts it MUST turn red
#   --baseline F   the pre-fix build for --control (default: newest js\main.js.bak-*-jsongroup)
#   --app DIR      where the libs + main.css come from (default: the live webroot)
#   --scn a,b      a subset of scenarios;  --keep keeps the staging dir
#
# Headless Edge over CDP; stages into %TEMP%; writes nothing to the webroot.
# Needs Python 3 + websocket-client (py -3 -m pip install websocket-client).
# =============================================================================
